  "claim_short": "Let E -> B be a rank-k Euclidean vector bundle. If E^(direct-sum (m-1)) has a nowhere-zero section, then there is no positive universal simultaneous Tukey-depth bound for m mass assignments on E. More precisely, for every eta>0 there are m continuous fiberwise Gaussian mass assignments such that, at every b in B and every x in E_b, at least one of the m measures has depth below eta at x.",
